---
import LibraryLayout from "../../layouts/LibraryLayout.astro";
import "../../styles/section-pages.css";
---
<LibraryLayout activeSection="terms" title="Website Terms of Use — Ridwanah" description="Read the basic terms that apply to use of the Ridwanah educational website.">
  <div id="top" class="policy-page">
    <div class="library-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Terms of use</span></div>
    <section class="policy-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> USING RIDWANAH</div>
      <h1>Clear information.<br /><em>Responsible use.</em></h1>
      <p>These plain-language terms describe the intended use of the current Ridwanah educational website. They are not a substitute for formal legal terms reviewed for the final operating entity and jurisdiction.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="policy-content">
      <section><h2>Educational purpose</h2><p>You may use this website to read general health education, browse selected public-health news summaries and access external educational resources. The site is not a medical service or emergency facility.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Use information responsibly</h2><p>Do not rely on website content as a personal diagnosis, treatment plan or substitute for professional healthcare. Check original sources and current local guidance before acting on health information.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Content and external resources</h2><p>Ridwanah provides links to third-party websites and videos for context. Those resources are operated by their respective publishers, who are responsible for their content, availability and policies. A link does not automatically mean Ridwanah endorses the publisher or every statement it makes.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Intellectual property</h2><p>Ridwanah’s original text, brand assets and site design should not be copied or represented as another organisation’s work without permission. Third-party names, videos, logos and materials remain the property of their respective owners. Follow the source’s licensing and reuse rules.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Availability and updates</h2><p>We may update, correct, suspend or remove pages as content and technical requirements change. We do not guarantee uninterrupted availability or that every external resource will remain accessible.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Changes and legal review</h2><p>These terms must be reviewed and adapted by a qualified legal professional before commercial operation or launch under a registered organisation. Applicable law, the responsible operator and any required contact details must be confirmed rather than assumed.</p></section>
      <div class="policy-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/privacy">Read the privacy notice <span>↗</span></a><a class="policy-text-link" href="/disclaimer">Health disclaimer <span>→</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</LibraryLayout>
